<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [159].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>159&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;THERMOCOCCUS CELER MEDIUM</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Modified Brock's salt base solution (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=165">165</a>)   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> NaCl                                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;40.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Yeast extract (BD-Difco)                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;2.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Sulfur (powder)                                        </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O                                   </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix ingredients, except yeast extract, sulfur and Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O,      adjust pH to 5.8 with H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>, and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub>      atmosphere.   Separately autoclave yeast extract as a 10%      solution under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere.   Steam sulfur for 3 hr on each of       3 successive days.   Neutralize Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O as a      5% solution, and autoclave under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere.   Aseptically      and anaerobically add the yeast extract solution and sulfur to the medium.      Prior to inoculation, add the sterile Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution, and       readjust pH to 5.8, if necessary.       <br>
